CHAPTER 1: INTRODUCTION
1.1 Introduction
Water is one of the most important natural resources required for human life. In homes, schools, offices, and industries, water is commonly stored in overhead tanks and storage containers.
Traditional water-level monitoring methods require people to manually check the tank. Sometimes, people forget to switch off the water pump, which causes water overflow and wastage.
To overcome this problem, an IoT Based Smart Water Level Monitoring System is developed. It automatically measures the water level using an ultrasonic sensor and provides indications through LEDs and a buzzer.
This system helps users monitor the water level easily and reduces the need for manual checking.
1.2 Problem Statement
Traditional water tanks do not always have an automatic monitoring facility. Users often face problems such as:
•	Water overflow due to overfilling.
•	Wastage of water.
•	Manual checking of tank levels.
•	Difficulty in identifying the remaining water.
•	Unnecessary time and effort.
Therefore, an automated water-level monitoring system is required.
1.3 Objectives
The main objectives of this project are:
1.	To monitor the water level automatically.
2.	To measure the distance between the sensor and the water surface.
3.	To display water-level conditions using LEDs.
4.	To generate an alert when the tank is almost full.
5.	To reduce water wastage and overflow.
6.	To develop a low-cost and user-friendly monitoring system.
7.	To provide a foundation for future IoT-based remote monitoring.
1.4 Scope of the Project
This project can be used in:
•	Residential water tanks.
•	Schools and colleges.
•	Office buildings.
•	Small industries.
•	Water storage containers.
•	Agricultural water storage systems.
