2.2 Description of Hardware Components
1. NodeMCU ESP8266
NodeMCU ESP8266 is a microcontroller development board with built-in Wi-Fi connectivity. It 
receives data from the ultrasonic sensor, processes the information, and controls the LEDs and buzzer.
2. HC-SR04 Ultrasonic Sensor
The HC-SR04 is an ultrasonic distance-measuring sensor. It sends ultrasonic sound waves and receives the reflected waves from the water surface.
It contains four pins:
•	VCC
•	TRIG
•	ECHO
•	GND
It is used to calculate the distance between the sensor and the water surface.
3. LEDs
LEDs are used to indicate the water level.
•	Red LED: Low water level.
•	Yellow LED: Medium water level.
•	Green LED: High water level.
4. Buzzer
The buzzer produces an audible alert when the water level reaches the defined full-tank warning limit.
5. Breadboard
A breadboard is used to connect the electronic components without soldering.
6. Jumper Wires
Jumper wires are used to establish electrical connections between the NodeMCU, sensor, LEDs, and buzzer.
