5.2 Expected Results
The system detects changes in the water level and displays the corresponding indication.
When the tank is almost empty, the red LED glows. When the water reaches the medium level, the yellow LED glows. At a high water level, the green LED glows.
When the water level reaches approximately 90%, the buzzer produces an alert.
The readings can also be observed through the Arduino Serial Monitor.
5.3 Advantages
1.	Reduces water wastage.
2.	Provides automatic water-level monitoring.
3.	Easy to understand and operate.
4.	Low-cost project.
5.	Requires less maintenance.
6.	Saves time and human effort.
7.	Can be extended with Wi-Fi-based monitoring.
5.4 Limitations
1.	The sensor requires proper installation.
2.	Water splashes may affect readings.
3.	The system requires a continuous power supply.
4.	Incorrect sensor positioning may produce inaccurate results.
5.	The basic implementation displays readings locally and does not yet provide remote mobile notifications.
