CHAPTER 8: CONCLUSION
The IoT Based Smart Water Level Monitoring System provides a simple and effective method of monitoring the water level in a storage tank.
The project uses an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor to measure the distance between the sensor and the water surface. The NodeMCU ESP8266 processes the sensor readings and controls the LEDs and buzzer according to the water level.
This system helps reduce water wastage, prevents unnecessary overflow, and decreases the need for manual monitoring.
The project is economical, easy to implement, and can be further improved by adding mobile application support, cloud connectivity, and automatic water pump control.
